# Pi-hole gravity blocklists. One URL per line; '#' comments and blanks ignored.
# Load with `make blocklists` after `make up` (idempotent - safe to re-run).
# Pi-hole also refreshes these automatically via its built-in weekly cron.

# ── OISD Big ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ads, trackers, malware, phishing, telemetry, cryptojacking, scam/spam.
# Already consolidates many upstream lists (incl. Steven Black's sources).
https://big.oisd.nl

# ── Steven Black ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Consolidated hosts (adaway, mvps, malwaredomainlist, someonewhocares, ...).
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StevenBlack/hosts/master/hosts

# ── notracking ── DISABLED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unmaintained (last updated 2022) and largely redundant with OISD.
# Uncomment if you specifically want it.
#https://raw.githubusercontent.com/notracking/hosts-blocklists/master/hostnames.txt

# ── EasyList ── DISABLED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Adblock-Plus *filter* list (cosmetic/URL-path rules) built for browser ad
# blockers, not DNS. Pi-hole can only use its small domain subset and it risks
# false positives. Prefer OISD for DNS-level ad blocking. Uncomment at your risk.
#https://easylist.to/easylist/easylist.txt

# ── NextDNS "Ads & Trackers" ── UNAVAILABLE ──────────────────────────────────
# No public Pi-hole URL exists; it is served only inside NextDNS's resolver.
# OISD + Steven Black above cover the same ground.
